gcshape 1  into:/GraphCodeShape/Presets  smooth:0.5  shade:40

# WOOD RUIN — L3 Parts: broken wooden structure modules that swap in place for intact ones, each with
# the debris its break left. `Docs/GC-SHAPE-DAMAGE-KIT.md` §2.0, §3.3, §4.2, §10 and §12; W1 rounds 3-6 in `Docs/GC-SHAPE-DAMAGE-KIT-ROUNDS.md`.
#
#   Ruin = shape('/GraphCodeShape/Presets/WoodRuin', Face = $Oak, Broken = $OakTorn)
#   Porch = mesh() { add($Ruin.Deck, hole_rx=30.0, hole_ry=40.0, hole_x=60.0, noise=4) }
#
# GENERATED by `Content/__MCPTests/DamageKit/gen/genwoodruin.py` (and `genwreck.py`); edit the generators, never this file.
#
# THE FLOOR DECK MODULE (`Deck`). Boards run along +Y (their grain, the Damage frame) on joists along X; the origin is
# the module's top-surface min corner: boards' top near z = 0, joists below. A state is a table of knob values (the
# wrapper entries below); every build line carries `[bounds=(size_x, size_y, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]`, so a broken
# state swaps in for the intact one.
#
# HOW TO TURN IT (kit §11a): the six TOP-LEVEL knobs lead every kit file, named the same; everything after them is
# advanced. Every knob is clamped to its range inside the recipe (a value past it is clamped, never a broken mesh);
# the seeds `noise` and `fseed` are any integer. MATERIAL SLOTS (pass them to shape(...)): `Face` the boards' and
# joists' skin, `Broken` every torn face, `Nail` the stub's nail (`Block` is internal and deleted).
#   Ruin  = shape('/GraphCodeShape/Presets/WoodRuin', Face = $Oak, Broken = $OakTorn, Nail = $Iron)
#   Porch = mesh() { add($Ruin.Deck, size_x=240.0, damage=0.7, age=1.6, noise=4, budget=1) }
#
# THE AGED FLOOR (round 6, kit §12.3: nothing is a perfect rectangle): one layout from `fseed`, shared by every state,
# so the boards round a hole are the intact floor's own: lanes of varied width and gap, boards butt-joined over the
# inner joists at staggered places (never at a joist where the lane beside has a joint), every board TimberKit's
# `AgedBoard` recipe (its draws, worn section and `Age`, the deck holding yaw and crook inside the gaps), broken
# where the hole breaks it; a board that began on a rim joist ends there in its clean butt end or turns its whole end.
# THE HOLE (rounds 2-5), calibrated to real broken floors (`Docs/Research/real-broken-floors.md`).
#
# Deck's knobs (also DeckDebris's; Wreck's are listed above `Wreck`):
#   knob        default   range          unit      meaning
#   size_x      200.0     100-400        cm        the module across the boards (lanes are added or dropped; the pitch stays)
#   size_y      200.0     100-400        cm        the module along the boards (the joists respace: size_y / joists)
#   damage      1.0       0-1.6                    how broken: the hole is damage x (hole_rx, hole_ry); 0 the intact floor, 1 the default, 1.6 the most
#   age         1.0       0-2                      how worn: every imperfection of the boards and joists x age (1 + age) / 2 (0 new and true, 1 aged, 2 decayed: three times the aged ranges)
#   noise       1         -              seed      the hole's seed: where it falls, every break, every fate
#   budget      1         0-2                      0 game (arrises chamfered, their round baked), 1 high (worn rounds), 2 ultra (8 segments, finer breaks)
#   board_w     14.0      8-25           cm        the boards' nominal width: the lanes' pitch
#   board_t     1.9       1.2-5          cm        the boards' thickness
#   board_gap   0.3       0.1-1          cm        the nominal gap the pitch allows for
#   joists      5         3-8            count     joists under the module
#   joist_w     3.8       3-10           cm        the joists' width
#   joist_d     18.4      10-30          cm        the joists' depth
#   fseed       5         -              seed      the floor's seed: lanes, joints, every board's draws; every state shares it, so a broken state swaps in
#   wjit        0.05      0-0.1          x pitch   each boundary between lanes moves up to this either way (lane widths +-2 wjit)
#   gapmin      0.1       0-1            cm        the narrowest gap between two lanes
#   gapmax      0.8       0-2            cm        the widest gap between two lanes (at age 1)
#   egap        0.3       0-1            cm        the gap at the module's sides (half each side, so modules tile)
#   einset      0.05      0.02-0.3       cm        the boards' ends in from the module's ends
#   pnone       0.2       0-1            share     the lanes with no butt joint
#   ptwo        0.35      0-1            share     the jointed lanes with a second joint two joists on
#   bgmin       0.15      0.05-1         cm        the narrowest butt joint
#   bgmax       0.4       0.05-2         cm        the widest butt joint
#   bvar        0.015     0-0.05         x width   a board narrower than its lane by up to this
#   tvar        0.05      0-0.15         x thick   each board thicker or thinner by up to this
#   yaw         0.5       0-1.5          deg       each board turned 0.4-1 x this, held inside the gaps round it
#   lift        0.15      0-0.6          cm        each board raised by up to this (never sunk into its joists)
#   cup         0.3       0-1            cm        each board's edges this far off its middle (up on 3 boards of 4)
#   bow         0.25      0-1            cm        each board's middle raised up to this between its nails
#   crook       0.25      0-1            cm        each board's middle sideways up to this
#   endsq       1.5       0-5            deg       each butt joint up to this off square (both boards follow it)
#   wear        0.5       0-1.5          cm        the worn top arrises' mean radius (x 0.3 + 0.7 age)
#   wearvar     0.6       0-1            x wear    how much the radius varies, board to board and along a board
#   jvw         0.05      0-0.15         x         each joist's width +- this
#   jvd         0.03      0-0.1          x         each joist's depth +- this
#   jsag        0.4       0-2            cm        each joist sags 0.4-1 x this
#   jcrook      0.3       0-1            cm        each joist crooked sideways up to this
#   shade       0.15      0-0.6          x         each board's state: darkened by up to this (x the age spread) in vertex colour R
#   hole_x      0.5       0-1            x size_x  the hole's centre across the boards, a share of the module
#   hole_y      0.5       0-1            x size_y  the hole's centre along the boards, a share of the module
#   hole_rx     55.0      5-150          cm        the half-span across the boards at damage 1 (Wreck: the collapse's)
#   hole_ry     35.0      5-100          cm        the half-length along the boards at damage 1
#   cvar        25.0      0-50           cm        each seed moves the centre up to this
#   svar        0.25      0-0.5          x         each seed scales the span and length by up to this
#   jump        0.1       0-1            share     of the boards, where a rim steps a bay to the next joist
#   midbay      0.42      0-1            share     of the level and cracked ends, those 5-15 cm off their joist
#   pshort      0.4       0-1            share     of those, the ones short of the joist (the joist left bare)
#   gmin        18.0      5-60           cm        the least board removed between a board's two ends
#   survive     2         0-2            count     the most boards that survive across the hole (each seed draws 0 to this)
#   ssag        2.0       0-6            cm        a survivor's sag into each bay
#   scrack      6.0       0-20           deg       a survivor's crack, opening each side
#   plevel      0.6       0-1            share     ends left level
#   phang       0.25      0-1            share     ends hanging hlo-hhi
#   pcrack      0.1       0-1            share     ends cracked and sagging clo-chi (the rest are steep)
#   hlo         15.0      0-80           deg       a hanging end's least turn
#   hhi         45.0      0-85           deg       a hanging end's most turn
#   clo         5.0       0-40           deg       a cracked end's least turn
#   chi         15.0      0-45           deg       a cracked end's most turn
#   slo         60.0      30-85          deg       a steep end's least turn
#   shi         80.0      30-88          deg       a steep end's most turn
#   stub        1         0-1            flag      one board near an end of the span hangs a stub from one nail
#   nmin        10.0      4-30           cm        the stub's least length
#   nmax        15.0      4-30           cm        the stub's most length
#   nlo         35.0      10-80          deg       the stub's least turn
#   nhi         45.0      10-85          deg       the stub's most turn
#   rimfrag     1         0-1            flag      a loose torn piece lying on one rim's boards
#   rimchips    4         0-10           count     chips beside it
#   long        0.5       0-1            share     breaks that are long (splintered) rather than short
#   deep        0.75      0.2-1.5        x width   a short break's spire depth
#   ldeep       1.3       0.4-2.5        x width   a long break's spire depth
#   splint      1.0       0.2-2          x         the long-splinter scale
#   slant       12.0      0-20           deg       each break's slant, either way (Damage's limit is about 20)
#   grain       0.24      0.1-0.6        x width   a break's spire width
#   lean        1.6       0-3            x thick   how far a break's top face tears from its bottom
#   horn        0.3       0-1            share     breaks with one horn
#   rings       0         0-1            flag      Damage's partition: 0 rows x columns, 1 rings x rays
#   torn        0.85      0-1                      round 9's blunt torn ends on short breaks
#   torntilt    0.15      0-0.5                    how far each torn end tilts
#   tornrib     1         0-1            flag      one ribbon length per bundle
#   tornsep     0.15      0-0.5                    how deep the cracks between bundles run
#   uvbox       1         0-1            flag      each piece mapped by one box after its breaks
#   detail      0.14      0.06-0.4       cm        a board break's point spacing (under 0.06 Damage's chew refuses)
#   hdetail     0.12      0.06-0.4       cm        a hinge's or a survivor crack's point spacing
#   jdetail     0.3       0.1-0.6        cm        a snapped joist's point spacing
#   tile        100.0     20-400         cm        one UV tile
#   aspect      1.0       0.25-4                   along-grain tile over across
#
# DeckDebris adds:
#   knob        default   range          unit      meaning
#   dmin        10.0      4-60           cm        a removed run shorter than this is lost (WreckDebris: lies as crumbs)
#   dshort      0.0       0-120          cm        a fragment shorter than this takes plain fresh ends
#   frag        80.0      30-200         cm        the fragments' mean length
#   grow        1.3       1-2.5          x         the pile's footprint over the hole's
#   tumble      8.0       0-45           deg       each fragment tumbled up to this
#   tilt        0.35      0-1            share     fragments lying tilted, one end raised
#   edge        0.12      0-1            share     fragments lying on edge
#   lsplit      0.3       0-1            share     fragments split along their length
#   splinters   0.3       0-1            share     boards that leave a loose splinter
#   ddetail     0.07      0.06-0.3       cm        the fragments' point spacing
#
# THE COLLAPSE (`Wreck`, `SM_WoodDeck_Wrecked`): see its own header below (`gen/genwreck.py`).
#
# THE DEBRIS (`DeckDebris`): what the hole lost, on its own ground plane (z = 0 is the floor below; place it at the
# module's X/Y; its build line takes a 20 cm margin round the module, kit 2.0.3). Each lane's removed run of `dmin` cm
# or more becomes 1-3 aged fragments whose ends are the rim's own breaks, tooth into socket (a butt end sawn), and
# fresh breaks between them, scattered over the hole's footprint grown `grow` times, stacked. Game tier only.
#
# BUDGET TIERS (kit §12.1, §8a item 6): one recipe, the knob `budget`. Each state's `SM_WoodDeck_<State>` is the light
# game tier, `[triangles=N, maps=(normal, ao), from=$<State>High]` (budget 0: arrises chamfered, their round and the
# fine break baked); `SM_WoodDeck_<State>_High` (budget 1) and `_Ultra` (budget 2: 8 segments along a board; its
# wrapper also passes every break's point spacing 0.6 x) the full-detail grades; their size is the author's choice.

build {
  SM_WoodDeck_Intact           = $DeckIntactGame   [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=2000, maps=(normal, ao), from=$DeckIntactHigh, resolution=1024, supersample=1]
  SM_WoodDeck_Intact_High      = $DeckIntactHigh   [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Intact_Ultra     = $DeckIntactUltra  [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken           = $DeckBrokenGame   [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=9000, maps=(normal, ao), from=$DeckBrokenHigh, resolution=1024, supersample=1]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken_High      = $DeckBrokenHigh   [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken_Ultra     = $DeckBrokenUltra  [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Wrecked          = $DeckWreckedGame   [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=12000, maps=(normal, ao), from=$DeckWreckedHigh, resolution=1024, supersample=1]
  SM_WoodDeck_Wrecked_High     = $DeckWreckedHigh   [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Wrecked_Ultra    = $DeckWreckedUltra  [bounds=(200, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken_300       = $DeckBroken300Game   [bounds=(300, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=10000, maps=(normal, ao), from=$DeckBroken300High, resolution=1024, supersample=1]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken_300_High  = $DeckBroken300High   [bounds=(300, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken_300_Ultra = $DeckBroken300Ultra  [bounds=(300, 200, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0)]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken_Debris     = $DeckBrokenDebris     [bounds=(240, 240, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=10000]
  SM_WoodDeck_Wrecked_Debris    = $DeckWreckedDebris    [bounds=(240, 240, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=12000]
  SM_WoodDeck_Broken_300_Debris = $DeckBroken300Debris  [bounds=(340, 240, *), pivot=(0, 0, 0), triangles=10000]
}

Face   = material()
Broken = material()
Nail   = material()
Block  = material()
Dmg    = shape('/GraphCodeShape/Presets/Damage')
Debris = shape('/GraphCodeShape/Presets/Debris', Face = $Face, Broken = $Broken)
Kit    = shape('/GraphCodeShape/Presets/TimberKit', Face = $Face, Broken = $Broken)

# ---- blanks ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# a plain board in the Damage frame: centred on x, bottom on z = 0, y from 0 to length; its grain +Y (the snapped
# joist's halves are built from it)
Plank = mesh(width=14.0, thick=1.9, length=200.0, tile=100.0, aspect=1.0) {
  rect(w=$width, h=$length)
  extrude(height=$thick)
  place(by=(0.0, 0.5 * $length, 0.0))
  uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, 1, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile))
  material($Face)
}

# a straight path along +Y, 0 to 100 cm in 41 stations: a board swept along it has rings to bend
Run100 = plane() { points((0.0, 0.0, 0.0), (0.0, 2.5, 0.0), (0.0, 5.0, 0.0), (0.0, 7.5, 0.0), (0.0, 10.0, 0.0), (0.0, 12.5, 0.0), (0.0, 15.0, 0.0), (0.0, 17.5, 0.0), (0.0, 20.0, 0.0), (0.0, 22.5, 0.0), (0.0, 25.0, 0.0), (0.0, 27.5, 0.0), (0.0, 30.0, 0.0), (0.0, 32.5, 0.0), (0.0, 35.0, 0.0), (0.0, 37.5, 0.0), (0.0, 40.0, 0.0), (0.0, 42.5, 0.0), (0.0, 45.0, 0.0), (0.0, 47.5, 0.0), (0.0, 50.0, 0.0), (0.0, 52.5, 0.0), (0.0, 55.0, 0.0), (0.0, 57.5, 0.0), (0.0, 60.0, 0.0), (0.0, 62.5, 0.0), (0.0, 65.0, 0.0), (0.0, 67.5, 0.0), (0.0, 70.0, 0.0), (0.0, 72.5, 0.0), (0.0, 75.0, 0.0), (0.0, 77.5, 0.0), (0.0, 80.0, 0.0), (0.0, 82.5, 0.0), (0.0, 85.0, 0.0), (0.0, 87.5, 0.0), (0.0, 90.0, 0.0), (0.0, 92.5, 0.0), (0.0, 95.0, 0.0), (0.0, 97.5, 0.0), (0.0, 100.0, 0.0)) }

# the ground a debris pile falls on (scaled to the hole's footprint), deleted again by its handle
Disc = mesh() {
  circle(radius=1.0, segments=32)
  extrude(height=1.0)
}

# a nail's shank, 0.3 cm square, from z = 0 down to -len
NailRod = mesh(len=4.5) {
  rect(w=0.3, h=0.3)
  extrude(height=$len)
  place(by=(0.0, 0.0, -$len))
  uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, 1, 0), scale=(100.0, 100.0, 100.0))
  material($Nail)
}

# ---- the aged floor's pieces (round 6) -----------------------------------------------------------------

# ONE BOARD OF THE FLOOR, or the piece of it a break leaves: TimberKit's `AgedBoard` recipe (its draws, its worn
# section, its `Age`), keyed `noise * 1009 + index` as AgedBoard is, with the floor's rules over the drawn numbers
# (`floor_rules` in the generator). In the board's own frame (centred on x, bottom on z = 0, y from 0 to `length`).
# Each end may be cut at `c0` / `c1` (k = 1 a deck break, keeping the side toward the board's middle; 2 the hinge's
# torn line, its level side; 3 its complement, the turned side); the piece is then moved so `pivot` is its origin
# (a turned piece turns about its hinge) and, on the stub, a nail goes in 1.2 cm past it.
DeckBoard = mesh(width=14.0, thick=1.9, length=200.0, wvar=0.015, tvar=0.05, lvar=0.0, yaw=0.5, lift=0.15, cup=0.3, bow=0.25, crook=0.25, endsq=1.5, wear=0.5, wearvar=0.6, arris=3, seg=4, room=0.2, g0=0.1, ea0=0.0, g1=0.1, ea1=0.0, k0=0, c0=0.0, k1=0, c1=200.0, pivot=0.0, deep=0.75, grain=0.24, lean=1.6, ang=0.0, splint=0.8, vdep=0.7, horn=0.0, rings=0, torn=0.0, torntilt=0.0, tornrib=0, tornsep=0.15, uvbox=1, detail=0.12, nb=1, hinge=0.0, hdetail=0.12, nh=1, nail=0, shade=0.0, tile=100.0, aspect=1.0, noise=1, index=0) {
  $K = $noise * 1009 + $index
  $ad1 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 20.4) * 43758.5453
  $ad1 = $ad1 - floor($ad1)
  $ad2 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 37.7) * 43758.5453
  $ad2 = $ad2 - floor($ad2)
  $ad3 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 55.0) * 43758.5453
  $ad3 = $ad3 - floor($ad3)
  $ad4 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 72.3) * 43758.5453
  $ad4 = $ad4 - floor($ad4)
  $ad5 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 89.6) * 43758.5453
  $ad5 = $ad5 - floor($ad5)
  $ad6 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 106.9) * 43758.5453
  $ad6 = $ad6 - floor($ad6)
  $ad7 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 124.2) * 43758.5453
  $ad7 = $ad7 - floor($ad7)
  $ad8 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 141.5) * 43758.5453
  $ad8 = $ad8 - floor($ad8)
  $ad9 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 158.8) * 43758.5453
  $ad9 = $ad9 - floor($ad9)
  $ad10 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 176.1) * 43758.5453
  $ad10 = $ad10 - floor($ad10)
  $ad11 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 193.4) * 43758.5453
  $ad11 = $ad11 - floor($ad11)
  $ad12 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 210.7) * 43758.5453
  $ad12 = $ad12 - floor($ad12)
  $ad13 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 228.0) * 43758.5453
  $ad13 = $ad13 - floor($ad13)
  $ad14 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 245.3) * 43758.5453
  $ad14 = $ad14 - floor($ad14)
  $ad15 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 262.6) * 43758.5453
  $ad15 = $ad15 - floor($ad15)
  $ad16 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 279.9) * 43758.5453
  $ad16 = $ad16 - floor($ad16)
  $ad17 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 297.2) * 43758.5453
  $ad17 = $ad17 - floor($ad17)
  $ad18 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 314.5) * 43758.5453
  $ad18 = $ad18 - floor($ad18)
  $ad19 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 331.8) * 43758.5453
  $ad19 = $ad19 - floor($ad19)
  $ad20 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 349.1) * 43758.5453
  $ad20 = $ad20 - floor($ad20)
  $Wd = $width * (1 + $wvar * (2 * $ad1 - 1))
  $Td = $thick * (1 + $tvar * (2 * $ad2 - 1))
  $Ld = $length * (1 + $lvar * (2 * $ad3 - 1))
  $yw = $yaw * (0.4 + 0.6 * $ad4) * (2 * floor(2 * $ad5) - 1)
  $lf = $lift * (2 * $ad6 - 1)
  $cp = $cup * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad7) * (1 - 2 * clamp(ceil($ad8 - 0.75), 0, 1))
  $bw = $bow * (2 * $ad9 - 1)
  $ck = $crook * (2 * $ad10 - 1)
  $e0 = $endsq * (2 * $ad11 - 1)
  $e1 = $endsq * (2 * $ad12 - 1)
  $rcap = min(0.3 * $Wd, 0.4 * $Td)
  $ra = min(max($wear * (1 + $wearvar * (2 * $ad13 - 1)), 0.1 * $wear), $rcap)
  $rb = min(max($wear * (1 + $wearvar * (2 * $ad14 - 1)), 0.1 * $wear), $rcap)
  $rc = min(0.35 * $wear * (0.6 + 0.8 * $ad15), $rcap)
  $rd = min(0.35 * $wear * (0.6 + 0.8 * $ad16), $rcap)
  $rm = max($ra, $rb)
  $wa = min($wearvar, 0.8) * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad17)
  $wb = min($wearvar, 0.8) * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad18)
  $ph = 360 * $ad19
  $fr = 0.6 + 1.2 * $ad20
  $lf = abs($lf) + max(-$cp, 0)
  $bw = abs($bw)
  $e0 = $ea0
  $e1 = $ea1
  $kq = min(1, $room / max(0.5 * $Ld * abs(sin($yw)) + abs($ck), 0.001), max(min($g0, $g1) - 0.01, 0) / max(0.5 * $Wd * abs(sin($yw)), 0.0001))
  $yw = $yw * $kq
  $ck = $ck * $kq
  if ($arris > 1.5) {
    add($Kit.AgedSec3, w=$Wd, t=$Td, a=$ra, b=$rb, c=$rc, d=$rd, seg=$seg, scale=(1.0, $Ld / 100.0, 1.0))
  } else {
    add($Kit.AgedSec1, w=$Wd, t=$Td, a=$ra, b=$rb, c=$rc, d=$rd, seg=$seg, scale=(1.0, $Ld / 100.0, 1.0))
  }
  if ($k0 * clamp(ceil(($c0) - (0.5)), 0, 1) * clamp(ceil(($Ld - 0.5) - ($c0)), 0, 1) > 0.5) {
    if ($k0 > 2.5) {
      $Dmg.SnapOff(width=$Wd, thick=$Td, deep=$hinge, lean=0.6, wander=0.05, layers=2, fray=0.0, loss=0.0, chew=0.0, thin=0.0, detail=$hdetail, noise=$nh, origin=(0.0, $c0, 0.0), rotation=(0.0, 0.0, 0.0), uvfit=2 * $uvbox, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
    } else {
      if ($k0 > 1.5) {
        $Dmg.Snap(width=$Wd, thick=$Td, deep=$hinge, lean=0.6, wander=0.05, layers=2, fray=0.0, loss=0.0, chew=0.0, thin=0.0, detail=$hdetail, noise=$nh, origin=(0.0, $c0, 0.0), rotation=(0.0, 0.0, 180.0), uvfit=2 * $uvbox, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
      } else {
        $Dmg.Snap(width=$Wd, thick=$Td, deep=$deep, grain=$grain, lean=$lean, layers=2, rings=$rings, uneven=0.4, rough=1.0, long=$splint, vdep=$vdep, horn=$horn, torn=$torn, torntilt=$torntilt, tornrib=$tornrib, tornsep=$tornsep, loss=0.0, chew=0.05, detail=$detail, noise=$nb, origin=(0.0, $c0, 0.0), rotation=(0.0, 0.0, 180.0 + $ang), uvfit=2 * $uvbox, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
      }
    }
  }
  if ($k1 * clamp(ceil(($c1) - (0.5)), 0, 1) * clamp(ceil(($Ld - 0.5) - ($c1)), 0, 1) > 0.5) {
    if ($k1 > 2.5) {
      $Dmg.SnapOff(width=$Wd, thick=$Td, deep=$hinge, lean=0.6, wander=0.05, layers=2, fray=0.0, loss=0.0, chew=0.0, thin=0.0, detail=$hdetail, noise=$nh, origin=(0.0, $c1, 0.0), rotation=(0.0, 0.0, 180.0), uvfit=2 * $uvbox, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
    } else {
      if ($k1 > 1.5) {
        $Dmg.Snap(width=$Wd, thick=$Td, deep=$hinge, lean=0.6, wander=0.05, layers=2, fray=0.0, loss=0.0, chew=0.0, thin=0.0, detail=$hdetail, noise=$nh, origin=(0.0, $c1, 0.0), rotation=(0.0, 0.0, 0.0), uvfit=2 * $uvbox, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
      } else {
        $Dmg.Snap(width=$Wd, thick=$Td, deep=$deep, grain=$grain, lean=$lean, layers=2, rings=$rings, uneven=0.4, rough=1.0, long=$splint, vdep=$vdep, horn=$horn, torn=$torn, torntilt=$torntilt, tornrib=$tornrib, tornsep=$tornsep, loss=0.0, chew=0.05, detail=$detail, noise=$nb, origin=(0.0, $c1, 0.0), rotation=(0.0, 0.0, $ang), uvfit=2 * $uvbox, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
      }
    }
  }
  $cut = clamp($k0 + $k1, 0, 1)
  if ($cut > 0.5) {
    keep(largest)
  }
  $Kit.Age(w=$Wd, t=$Td, len=$Ld, cupv=$cp, bowv=$bw, crookv=$ck, e0=$e0, e1=$e1, yawv=$yw, liftv=$lf, rm=$rm, wa=$wa, wb=$wb, ph=$ph, fr=$fr)
  if ($cut > 0.5) {
    uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, 1, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile)) [!cut]
    if (1 > 0.5) {
      uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, 1, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile), offset=(0.37, 0.61)) [cut]
    }
    material($Face)
    material($Broken) [cut]
  } else {
    uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, 1, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile))
    material($Face)
  }
  # this board's state (fresher or darker): vertex colour R, one value a board, keyed as its draws are
  $sh = sin($K * 12.9898 + 4127.3) * 43758.5453
  $sh = $sh - floor($sh)
  colour(1 - $shade * $sh, channel=r)
  if ($nail > 0.5) {
    add($NailRod, len=4.5, at=(0.0, $pivot + 1.2, 0.0), join=none)
  }
  place(by=(0.0, -$pivot, 0.0))
}

# a joist of the floor, its own: width and depth varied, sagging a little and crooked a little along its length, its
# arrises eased; built along +Y, its top at z = 0 (the deck turns it to run along X under the boards)
DeckJoist = mesh(w=3.8, d=18.4, len=200.0, jvw=0.05, jvd=0.03, jsag=0.4, jcrook=0.3, arris=3, tile=100.0, aspect=1.0, noise=1, index=0) {
  $K = $noise * 1013 + $index
  $jq1 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 3011.3) * 43758.5453
  $jq1 = $jq1 - floor($jq1)
  $jq2 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 3127.9) * 43758.5453
  $jq2 = $jq2 - floor($jq2)
  $jq3 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 3251.7) * 43758.5453
  $jq3 = $jq3 - floor($jq3)
  $jq4 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 3389.3) * 43758.5453
  $jq4 = $jq4 - floor($jq4)
  $Jw = $w * (1 + $jvw * (2 * $jq1 - 1))
  $Jd = $d * (1 + $jvd * (2 * $jq2 - 1))
  if ($arris > 1.5) {
    add($Kit.AgedSec3, w=$Jw, t=$Jd, a=0.35, b=0.3, c=0.15, d=0.15, seg=8, scale=(1.0, $len / 100.0, 1.0))
  } else {
    add($Kit.AgedSec1, w=$Jw, t=$Jd, a=0.35, b=0.3, c=0.15, d=0.15, seg=2, scale=(1.0, $len / 100.0, 1.0))
  }
  $Kit.Age(w=$Jw, t=$Jd, len=$len, bowv=-$jsag * (0.4 + 0.6 * $jq3), crookv=$jcrook * (2 * $jq4 - 1))
  uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, 1, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile))
  material($Face)
  place(by=(0.0, 0.0, -$Jd))
}

# TimberKit's worn section (`AgedSec3`'s outline, read from its generator) swept along 40 stations: a board that bends
AgedRing = mesh(w=20.0, t=5.0, a=0.5, b=0.5, c=0.15, d=0.15) {
  points((-0.5 * $w + $d, 0.0), (0.0, 0.0), (0.5 * $w - $c, 0.0), (0.5 * $w, 0.364 * $c), (0.5 * $w, $t - $b), (0.5 * $w - 0.234 * $b, $t - 0.3572 * $b), (0.5 * $w - 0.3572 * $b, $t - 0.234 * $b), (0.5 * $w - $b, $t), (0.0, $t), (-0.5 * $w + $a, $t), (-0.5 * $w + 0.3572 * $a, $t - 0.234 * $a), (-0.5 * $w + 0.234 * $a, $t - 0.3572 * $a), (-0.5 * $w, $t - $a), (-0.5 * $w, 0.364 * $d), loop=true)
  sweep(along=$Run100)
}

# ONE BOARD OF A LANE THAT BENDS (round 6: an aged board, its own section, on 40 stations), placed at y = a0 in the
# module's frame along the board. `mode` 0, a SURVIVOR of the broken state: over the joist at y = yc the board is cracked
# on top (`crack` 1 on the board over it: a torn pair, `side` 1 the -Y half, -1 the +Y half) and each half sags into
# its bay, landing level on the next joist (z = -sig d over the joist, then -(Sk 27/4 u (1 - u)^2 + sa sin^2(180 u))
# across the clear span u = d / clr). `mode` 1, a board over the WRECKED state's snapped joist: it sags into the V,
# cracked UNDERNEATH at yc, z = -vq (v^2 - max(v - ease, 0)^2) / (2 ease) with v = 1 at the crack, 0 at the hinge.
BentBoard = mesh(width=14.0, thick=1.9, length=200.0, wvar=0.015, tvar=0.05, lvar=0.0, yaw=0.5, lift=0.15, cup=0.3, bow=0.25, crook=0.25, endsq=1.5, wear=0.5, wearvar=0.6, arris=3, seg=4, room=0.2, g0=0.1, ea0=0.0, g1=0.1, ea1=0.0, a0=0.0, mode=0, crack=0, side=1, yc=100.0, jw=3.8, clr=36.2, sig=0.1, Sk=0.5, sa=2.5, hl=38.1, vd=6.0, ease=0.3, hdetail=0.12, nc=1, shade=0.0, tile=100.0, aspect=1.0, noise=1, index=0) {
  $K = $noise * 1009 + $index
  $ad1 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 20.4) * 43758.5453
  $ad1 = $ad1 - floor($ad1)
  $ad2 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 37.7) * 43758.5453
  $ad2 = $ad2 - floor($ad2)
  $ad3 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 55.0) * 43758.5453
  $ad3 = $ad3 - floor($ad3)
  $ad4 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 72.3) * 43758.5453
  $ad4 = $ad4 - floor($ad4)
  $ad5 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 89.6) * 43758.5453
  $ad5 = $ad5 - floor($ad5)
  $ad6 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 106.9) * 43758.5453
  $ad6 = $ad6 - floor($ad6)
  $ad7 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 124.2) * 43758.5453
  $ad7 = $ad7 - floor($ad7)
  $ad8 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 141.5) * 43758.5453
  $ad8 = $ad8 - floor($ad8)
  $ad9 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 158.8) * 43758.5453
  $ad9 = $ad9 - floor($ad9)
  $ad10 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 176.1) * 43758.5453
  $ad10 = $ad10 - floor($ad10)
  $ad11 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 193.4) * 43758.5453
  $ad11 = $ad11 - floor($ad11)
  $ad12 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 210.7) * 43758.5453
  $ad12 = $ad12 - floor($ad12)
  $ad13 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 228.0) * 43758.5453
  $ad13 = $ad13 - floor($ad13)
  $ad14 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 245.3) * 43758.5453
  $ad14 = $ad14 - floor($ad14)
  $ad15 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 262.6) * 43758.5453
  $ad15 = $ad15 - floor($ad15)
  $ad16 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 279.9) * 43758.5453
  $ad16 = $ad16 - floor($ad16)
  $ad17 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 297.2) * 43758.5453
  $ad17 = $ad17 - floor($ad17)
  $ad18 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 314.5) * 43758.5453
  $ad18 = $ad18 - floor($ad18)
  $ad19 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 331.8) * 43758.5453
  $ad19 = $ad19 - floor($ad19)
  $ad20 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 349.1) * 43758.5453
  $ad20 = $ad20 - floor($ad20)
  $Wd = $width * (1 + $wvar * (2 * $ad1 - 1))
  $Td = $thick * (1 + $tvar * (2 * $ad2 - 1))
  $Ld = $length * (1 + $lvar * (2 * $ad3 - 1))
  $yw = $yaw * (0.4 + 0.6 * $ad4) * (2 * floor(2 * $ad5) - 1)
  $lf = $lift * (2 * $ad6 - 1)
  $cp = $cup * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad7) * (1 - 2 * clamp(ceil($ad8 - 0.75), 0, 1))
  $bw = $bow * (2 * $ad9 - 1)
  $ck = $crook * (2 * $ad10 - 1)
  $e0 = $endsq * (2 * $ad11 - 1)
  $e1 = $endsq * (2 * $ad12 - 1)
  $rcap = min(0.3 * $Wd, 0.4 * $Td)
  $ra = min(max($wear * (1 + $wearvar * (2 * $ad13 - 1)), 0.1 * $wear), $rcap)
  $rb = min(max($wear * (1 + $wearvar * (2 * $ad14 - 1)), 0.1 * $wear), $rcap)
  $rc = min(0.35 * $wear * (0.6 + 0.8 * $ad15), $rcap)
  $rd = min(0.35 * $wear * (0.6 + 0.8 * $ad16), $rcap)
  $rm = max($ra, $rb)
  $wa = min($wearvar, 0.8) * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad17)
  $wb = min($wearvar, 0.8) * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad18)
  $ph = 360 * $ad19
  $fr = 0.6 + 1.2 * $ad20
  $lf = abs($lf) + max(-$cp, 0)
  $bw = abs($bw)
  $e0 = $ea0
  $e1 = $ea1
  $kq = min(1, $room / max(0.5 * $Ld * abs(sin($yw)) + abs($ck), 0.001), max(min($g0, $g1) - 0.01, 0) / max(0.5 * $Wd * abs(sin($yw)), 0.0001))
  $yw = $yw * $kq
  $ck = $ck * $kq
  add($AgedRing, w=$Wd, t=$Td, a=$ra, b=$rb, c=$rc, d=$rd, scale=(1.0, $Ld / 100.0, 1.0))
  if ($crack > 0.5) {
    if ($side > 0) {
      $Dmg.Snap(width=$Wd, thick=$Td, deep=0.0, lean=0.6, wander=0.05, layers=2, fray=0.0, loss=0.0, chew=0.0, thin=0.0, detail=$hdetail, noise=$nc, origin=(0.0, $yc - $a0, 0.0), uvfit=0, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
    } else {
      $Dmg.SnapOff(width=$Wd, thick=$Td, deep=0.0, lean=0.6, wander=0.05, layers=2, fray=0.0, loss=0.0, chew=0.0, thin=0.0, detail=$hdetail, noise=$nc, origin=(0.0, $yc - $a0, 0.0), uvfit=0, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
    }
    keep(largest)
  }
  $Kit.Age(w=$Wd, t=$Td, len=$Ld, cupv=$cp, bowv=$bw, crookv=$ck, e0=$e0, e1=$e1, yawv=$yw, liftv=$lf, rm=$rm, wa=$wa, wb=$wb, ph=$ph, fr=$fr)
  place(by=(0.0, $a0, 0.0))
  if ($mode < 0.5) {
    $k1 = 6.75 * $Sk
    $k2 = 2 * 3.14159265 * $sa
    warp(by=(0.0, $side * point.z * (-$sig * clamp(ceil(-($side * ($yc - point.y) - 0.5 * $jw)), 0, 1) - (1 - clamp(ceil(-($side * ($yc - point.y) - 0.5 * $jw)), 0, 1)) * ($k1 * (1 - clamp(($side * ($yc - point.y) - 0.5 * $jw) / $clr, 0, 1)) * (1 - 3 * clamp(($side * ($yc - point.y) - 0.5 * $jw) / $clr, 0, 1)) + $k2 * sin(180 * clamp(($side * ($yc - point.y) - 0.5 * $jw) / $clr, 0, 1)) * cos(180 * clamp(($side * ($yc - point.y) - 0.5 * $jw) / $clr, 0, 1))) / $clr), -$sig * min($side * ($yc - point.y) - 0.5 * $jw, 0) - $k1 * clamp(($side * ($yc - point.y) - 0.5 * $jw) / $clr, 0, 1) * (1 - clamp(($side * ($yc - point.y) - 0.5 * $jw) / $clr, 0, 1)) * (1 - clamp(($side * ($yc - point.y) - 0.5 * $jw) / $clr, 0, 1)) - $sa * sin(180 * clamp(($side * ($yc - point.y) - 0.5 * $jw) / $clr, 0, 1)) * sin(180 * clamp(($side * ($yc - point.y) - 0.5 * $jw) / $clr, 0, 1))))
  } else {
    $vq = $vd / (1 - 0.5 * $ease)
    $ka = $vq / ($ease * $hl)
    warp(by=(0.0, $side * (point.z - $Td) * $ka * min(clamp(1 - $side * ($yc - point.y) / $hl, 0, 1), $ease), -$vq * (clamp(1 - $side * ($yc - point.y) / $hl, 0, 1) * clamp(1 - $side * ($yc - point.y) / $hl, 0, 1) - max(clamp(1 - $side * ($yc - point.y) / $hl, 0, 1) - $ease, 0) * max(clamp(1 - $side * ($yc - point.y) / $hl, 0, 1) - $ease, 0)) / (2 * $ease)))
  }
  if ($crack > 0.5) {
    uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, 1, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile)) [!cut]
    if (1 > 0.5) {
      uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, 1, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile), offset=(0.37, 0.61)) [cut]
    }
    material($Face)
    material($Broken) [cut]
  } else {
    uv(box, facing=(0, 0, 1), up=(0, 1, 0), scale=($aspect * $tile, $tile, $tile))
    material($Face)
  }
  $sh = sin($K * 12.9898 + 4127.3) * 43758.5453
  $sh = $sh - floor($sh)
  colour(1 - $shade * $sh, channel=r)
}

# half of a snapped joist in the Damage frame (grain +Y, depth up +Z): from its bearing (origin, bottom
# edge) to a `BeamBreak` at y = len (round 3: round 9's torn ends, as the deck passes them)
JoistEnd = mesh(len=100.0, w=3.8, d=18.4, detail=0.3, torn=0.0, torntilt=0.0, tornrib=0, tornsep=0.15, tile=100.0, aspect=1.0, noise=1) {
  add($Plank, width=$w, thick=$d, length=$len + 30.0, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
  $Dmg.BeamBreak(width=$w, thick=$d, torn=$torn, torntilt=$torntilt, tornrib=$tornrib, tornsep=$tornsep, detail=$detail, noise=$noise, origin=(0.0, $len, 0.0), uvfit=0, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
  keep(largest)
  material($Face)
  material($Broken) [cut]
}

# A FRAGMENT of a board (round 6: aged, the board's own section and wear), y from 0 to len: its -Y end the complement of
# the break `n0` (tooth into socket), its +Y end a fresh break `n1` or, `far` 1, the complement of the far rim's break,
# which was made turned 180 degrees; `saw0`/`saw1` 1 a sawn (butt) end instead; `split` 1 splits it along its length
# at `sx` of the width from its -X side and keeps the larger strip. q0/q1 are each break's lean (Damage's `lean`).
Frag = mesh(len=40.0, width=14.0, thick=1.9, wvar=0.015, tvar=0.05, lvar=0.0, yaw=0.0, lift=0.0, cup=0.3, bow=0.0, crook=0.0, endsq=0.0, wear=0.5, wearvar=0.6, arris=1, seg=1, length=40.0, noise=1, index=0, saw0=0, saw1=0, n0=1, l0=0.75, a0=0.0, r0=0.24, q0=1.6, s0=0.8, v0=0.7, h0=0.0, n1=2, l1=0.75, a1=0.0, r1=0.24, q1=1.6, s1=0.8, v1=0.7, h1=0.0, far=0, split=0, sx=0.5, tl=0.0, ed=0.0, detail=0.1, t0=0.0, t1=0.0, torntilt=0.0, tornrib=0, tornsep=0.15, tile=100.0, aspect=1.0) {
  $K = $noise * 1009 + $index
  $ad1 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 20.4) * 43758.5453
  $ad1 = $ad1 - floor($ad1)
  $ad2 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 37.7) * 43758.5453
  $ad2 = $ad2 - floor($ad2)
  $ad3 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 55.0) * 43758.5453
  $ad3 = $ad3 - floor($ad3)
  $ad4 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 72.3) * 43758.5453
  $ad4 = $ad4 - floor($ad4)
  $ad5 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 89.6) * 43758.5453
  $ad5 = $ad5 - floor($ad5)
  $ad6 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 106.9) * 43758.5453
  $ad6 = $ad6 - floor($ad6)
  $ad7 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 124.2) * 43758.5453
  $ad7 = $ad7 - floor($ad7)
  $ad8 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 141.5) * 43758.5453
  $ad8 = $ad8 - floor($ad8)
  $ad9 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 158.8) * 43758.5453
  $ad9 = $ad9 - floor($ad9)
  $ad10 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 176.1) * 43758.5453
  $ad10 = $ad10 - floor($ad10)
  $ad11 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 193.4) * 43758.5453
  $ad11 = $ad11 - floor($ad11)
  $ad12 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 210.7) * 43758.5453
  $ad12 = $ad12 - floor($ad12)
  $ad13 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 228.0) * 43758.5453
  $ad13 = $ad13 - floor($ad13)
  $ad14 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 245.3) * 43758.5453
  $ad14 = $ad14 - floor($ad14)
  $ad15 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 262.6) * 43758.5453
  $ad15 = $ad15 - floor($ad15)
  $ad16 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 279.9) * 43758.5453
  $ad16 = $ad16 - floor($ad16)
  $ad17 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 297.2) * 43758.5453
  $ad17 = $ad17 - floor($ad17)
  $ad18 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 314.5) * 43758.5453
  $ad18 = $ad18 - floor($ad18)
  $ad19 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 331.8) * 43758.5453
  $ad19 = $ad19 - floor($ad19)
  $ad20 = sin($K * 12.9898 + 349.1) * 43758.5453
  $ad20 = $ad20 - floor($ad20)
  $Wd = $width * (1 + $wvar * (2 * $ad1 - 1))
  $Td = $thick * (1 + $tvar * (2 * $ad2 - 1))
  $Ld = $length * (1 + $lvar * (2 * $ad3 - 1))
  $yw = $yaw * (0.4 + 0.6 * $ad4) * (2 * floor(2 * $ad5) - 1)
  $lf = $lift * (2 * $ad6 - 1)
  $cp = $cup * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad7) * (1 - 2 * clamp(ceil($ad8 - 0.75), 0, 1))
  $bw = $bow * (2 * $ad9 - 1)
  $ck = $crook * (2 * $ad10 - 1)
  $e0 = $endsq * (2 * $ad11 - 1)
  $e1 = $endsq * (2 * $ad12 - 1)
  $rcap = min(0.3 * $Wd, 0.4 * $Td)
  $ra = min(max($wear * (1 + $wearvar * (2 * $ad13 - 1)), 0.1 * $wear), $rcap)
  $rb = min(max($wear * (1 + $wearvar * (2 * $ad14 - 1)), 0.1 * $wear), $rcap)
  $rc = min(0.35 * $wear * (0.6 + 0.8 * $ad15), $rcap)
  $rd = min(0.35 * $wear * (0.6 + 0.8 * $ad16), $rcap)
  $rm = max($ra, $rb)
  $wa = min($wearvar, 0.8) * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad17)
  $wb = min($wearvar, 0.8) * (0.3 + 0.7 * $ad18)
  $ph = 360 * $ad19
  $fr = 0.6 + 1.2 * $ad20
  $ex0 = (1 - $saw0) * (0.4 * $l0 * $Wd * (1 + $s0 + $v0) + ($h0 + $q0) * $Td + 6.0)
  $ex1 = (1 - $saw1) * (0.4 * $l1 * $Wd * (1 + $s1 + $v1) + ($h1 + $q1) * $Td + 6.0)
  $Ld = $len + $ex0 + $ex1
  if ($arris > 1.5) {
    add($Kit.AgedSec3, w=$Wd, t=$Td, a=$ra, b=$rb, c=$rc, d=$rd, seg=$seg, scale=(1.0, $Ld / 100.0, 1.0), at=(0.0, -$ex0, 0.0))
  } else {
    add($Kit.AgedSec1, w=$Wd, t=$Td, a=$ra, b=$rb, c=$rc, d=$rd, seg=$seg, scale=(1.0, $Ld / 100.0, 1.0), at=(0.0, -$ex0, 0.0))
  }
  if ($saw0 < 0.5) {
    $Dmg.SnapOff(width=$Wd, thick=$Td, deep=$l0, grain=$r0, lean=$q0, layers=2, rings=0, uneven=0.4, rough=1.0, long=$s0, vdep=$v0, horn=$h0, torn=$t0, torntilt=$torntilt, tornrib=$tornrib, tornsep=$tornsep, loss=0.0, chew=0.05, detail=$detail, noise=$n0, origin=(0.0, 0.0, 0.0), rotation=(0.0, 0.0, $a0), uvfit=2, tile=$tile, aspect=$aspect)
  }
  if ($saw1 < 0.5) {
